      "genre": "说明文",
      "title": "An Accidental Invention",
      "body": "Many great things were invented by accident. The potato chip is one of them. It was invented in 1853 by a cook named George Crum. One day, a customer said his fried potatoes were too thick. Crum was not happy, so he cut the potatoes very thin and fried them. He thought the customer would hate them. But the customer loved them! Soon these thin, crispy chips became popular. Today, potato chips are eaten all over the world. This story shows that some of the best things are made by mistake. A small accident can change the world.",
